IMPORT prelude

-- Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Agency Act 2013 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the Act means for a person
-- who has, or cares for someone with, an asbestos-related or silica-related disease, and for any person the Agency deals
-- with: whether the national plans commit governments (ss 5A(2), 5B(2)); when the Agency must report on progress under the
-- plans and make the report public (s 8A(1), (3), (5)); whether the CEO can ask me for information, whether the notice is
-- made as the Act requires, whether I must answer, and whether another law stops me answering (s 14A); and, if I seek or
-- hold a place on the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Council (which s 32(3)(b) opens to people with these
-- diseases and their carers): eligibility (ss 31, 32, 34(3), (4)), term (s 33), pay (s 35), the disclosure rule (s 37(3)),
-- resignation (s 39) and termination (s 40).
--
-- The Act gives no one a claim, a payment or compensation. A person with an asbestos-related or silica-related disease meets
-- it only in the provisions above; compensation for dust diseases is in other Acts (see NOTES.md).
--
-- SEAT: the individual the Act is applied to -- a person with, or caring for someone with, an asbestos-related or
-- silica-related disease, or any person the Agency asks for information; and, in the situations marked, the same person as
-- a candidate for or member of the Council. Provisions addressed to the Agency, the CEO, the Council or the Minister are
-- encoded as what they mean for that person. Every belief, satisfaction or agreement the Act leaves to the CEO or the
-- Minister is asked as an input, never guessed.
--
-- Edition: the compilation registered as C2024C00186 (Compilation No. 4, compilation date 31 May 2024, including Act No. 27,
-- 2024; Federal Register of Legislation, retrieved 13 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2013A00058.txt. No instrument brought in (no rules under s 48 are deposited).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: see NOTES.md (Scope). In short: commencement, object, Crown and Territories (ss 1-5), the Agency's
-- constitution, functions, powers and constitutional limits (ss 6-9, beyond what s 14A and s 8A borrow), the CEO's office
-- (ss 10-24 except s 14A), staff (ss 25-27), the Council's functions and directions (ss 28-30A), the Chair's acting
-- appointment beyond s 34(1), leave (s 36), meetings (ss 41-41E), the finance law (s 41F), planning (ss 42-44), delegation,
-- review and rules (ss 46-48), and the copies of the s 8A report given to Ministers (s 8A(2), (4)).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the seat above with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Agency Act 2013 -- a person with, or caring for someone with, an asbestos- or silica-related disease`

§§ `Dates`

-- The built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL); no daydate import.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`asa days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`asa the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

§§ `The actors and acts the regulative rules name`

DECLARE `Agency party` IS ONE OF
    -- "the Agency" (s 3: the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Agency, s 6)
    `the Agency`
    -- the person in the seat
    `I, the person asked`

DECLARE `Agency act` IS ONE OF
    -- s 8A(1), (3): "prepare a written report relating to the progress made ..."
    `prepare the progress report`
    -- s 8A(5): "make each report ... publicly available"
    `make the report publicly available`
    -- s 14A(5): "comply with a request" (give the information asked for)
    `give the CEO the information asked for`
    -- a plain fact the regulative rules do not match: the day I look at where things stand
    `I check where things stand`

§§ `ss 5A(2), 5B(2) -- does the national plan commit governments to act`

-- s 5A(2) (and s 5B(2) in the same words for the Silica National Strategic Plan): "The plan referred to in subsection (1)
-- represents a commitment to implement an agreed set of strategic actions and national targets focussing on the priorities
-- referred to in subparagraphs (1)(b)(i) to (v) only if the plan has been agreed to by at least 6 of the governments of the
-- Commonwealth and each State and Territory."
-- "only if": fewer than 6 governments is JUST FALSE. Six or more is read as JUST TRUE (fork line: the condition is necessary;
-- s 5A(1) is the plan's definition and is taken as met by the plan with that name).
DECLARE `National plan` IS ONE OF
    `the Asbestos National Strategic Plan`
    `the Silica National Strategic Plan`

@export Does a national strategic plan on asbestos or silica represent a commitment by governments to carry out its agreed actions and targets?
GIVEN `which plan` IS A `National plan` @desc Which plan you are asking about: "the Asbestos National Strategic Plan" or "the Silica National Strategic Plan"
      `governments that have agreed to it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the governments of the Commonwealth, the States and the Territories have agreed to the plan (a whole number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the national plan commit governments question` MEANS
    IF `governments that have agreed to it` AT LEAST 6
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8A -- when the Agency must report on progress under the plans, and make the report public`

-- s 8A(1): "The Agency must, before the end of 31 December in each financial year, prepare a written report relating to the
-- progress made by the Commonwealth and State and Territory governments in implementing the Asbestos National Strategic Plan
-- during the previous financial year." s 8A(3): the same for the Silica National Strategic Plan.
-- The financial year runs 1 July to 30 June. The report on the year that ended on 30 June of year Y is due before the end of
-- 31 December of year Y. Time is counted in days from 1 July of year Y (day 0); 31 December is day 183 in every year, and
-- an act on day 183 is in time (WITHIN counts it).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Agency party` `Agency act`
`s 8A(1), (3) -- the Agency must prepare the progress report before the end of 31 December` MEANS
    PARTY `the Agency`
    MUST  `prepare the progress report`
    WITHIN 183
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Agency` BECAUSE "the progress report on the previous financial year was not prepared before the end of 31 December (s 8A(1), (3))"

-- s 8A(5): "The Agency must make each report prepared under subsection (1) or (3) publicly available." No time is set, so the
-- rule has no WITHIN: it waits until the report is made public.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Agency party` `Agency act`
`s 8A(5) -- the Agency must make the report publicly available` MEANS
    PARTY `the Agency`
    MUST  `make the report publicly available`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- The year in which the reported financial year ended (2025 for the year 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025).
GIVEN `the year the financial year ended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`asa the 1 July that starts the reporting year` `the year the financial year ended` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 `the year the financial year ended`

@export By when must the Agency prepare its report on governments' progress under the asbestos or silica national plan during a financial year?
GIVEN `which plan` IS A `National plan` @desc Which plan: "the Asbestos National Strategic Plan" or "the Silica National Strategic Plan"
      `the year the financial year ended` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year you want the report on ended (for 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025, enter 2025)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the Agency report on progress question` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 `the year the financial year ended`

DECLARE `Report timing` IS ONE OF
    `prepared in time (before the end of 31 December)`
    `prepared late (after 31 December)`
    `not prepared yet, and still not due`
    `not prepared yet, and overdue (31 December has passed)`

-- Worked through the s 8A(1), (3) rule: a report already prepared is traced on the day it was prepared; a report not yet
-- prepared is traced as if it were prepared today, which is in time exactly when it is not yet overdue.
@export Was, or is, the Agency's report on progress under the asbestos or silica national plan for a financial year on time?
GIVEN `which plan` IS A `National plan` @desc Which plan: "the Asbestos National Strategic Plan" or "the Silica National Strategic Plan"
      `the year the financial year ended` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the reported financial year ended (for 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025, enter 2025)
      `the report has been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Agency has prepared the written progress report on that financial year
      `the day it was prepared` IS A DATE @desc The day the Agency prepared the report (ignored if it has not been prepared), on or after 1 July of the year entered
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Report timing`
`Is the progress report on time question` MEANS
    IF `the report has been prepared`
    THEN IF `in time if prepared on` `the day it was prepared`
         THEN `prepared in time (before the end of 31 December)`
         ELSE `prepared late (after 31 December)`
    ELSE IF `in time if prepared on` `today`
         THEN `not prepared yet, and still not due`
         ELSE `not prepared yet, and overdue (31 December has passed)`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `in time if prepared on` `the day` MEANS
            CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 8A(1), (3) -- the Agency must prepare the progress report before the end of 31 December` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Agency` `prepare the progress report` (`asa days from` (`asa the 1 July that starts the reporting year` `the year the financial year ended`) `to` `the day`)))
            WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 8A(5): once a report is prepared, the Agency "must make" it publicly available. Before it is prepared there is no
-- report to publish and s 8A(5) says nothing: NOTHING.
@export Must the Agency make its progress report on the asbestos or silica national plan publicly available?
GIVEN `the report has been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Agency has prepared the progress report you are asking about
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Agency make the progress report public question` MEANS
    IF `the report has been prepared`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 14A -- the CEO asks me for information (if the Agency's CEO has written to you)`

-- s 14A(1): "This section applies to a person if: (a) the CEO believes on reasonable grounds that the person has information
-- that is relevant to the performance of any of the functions of the Agency referred to in paragraphs 8(1)(a), (b) and (g);
-- and (b) the CEO is satisfied that the information: (i) is necessary for the performance of that function; and (ii) is not
-- otherwise available to the CEO."
-- s 14A(2): "The CEO may, by written notice given to the person, request the person to give to the CEO, within the period and
-- in the manner and form specified in the notice, any such information."
-- The functions in s 8(1)(a), (b), (g): implementing, reviewing and publishing the National Strategic Plans, and collecting
-- and analysing data on preventing exposure to asbestos fibres or respirable crystalline silica.
-- "if" (s 14A(1)) and "by written notice" (s 14A(2)): a failed condition is JUST FALSE.
@export Can the CEO of the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Agency ask me for information?
GIVEN `the CEO believes on reasonable grounds I have relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO believes, on reasonable grounds, that you have information relevant to the Agency's work on the national asbestos and silica plans or its data on exposure (s 8(1)(a), (b), (g))
      `the CEO is satisfied the information is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO is satisfied the information is necessary for that work
      `the CEO is satisfied the information is not otherwise available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO is satisfied the information is not otherwise available to the CEO
      `the request is made by written notice given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request came to you as a written notice (a letter or an email), not only by phone or in person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the CEO ask me for information question` MEANS
    IF `s 14A reaches me and the request` `the CEO believes on reasonable grounds I have relevant information` `the CEO is satisfied the information is necessary` `the CEO is satisfied the information is not otherwise available` `the request is made by written notice given to me`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `believes` IS A BOOLEAN, `necessary` IS A BOOLEAN, `not otherwise available` IS A BOOLEAN, `written` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14A reaches me and the request` `believes` `necessary` `not otherwise available` `written` IF
        `believes`
    AND `necessary`
    AND `not otherwise available`
    AND `written`

-- s 14A(3): "A period specified under subsection (2) must not be shorter than 14 days after the notice is given."
-- Read with s 36 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (a period after a day excludes that day): the last day a notice may
-- set is no earlier than the 14th day after the day it is given. Given on 1 March 2026, the earliest last day is 15 March.
@export If the Agency's CEO gives me a notice asking for information, what is the earliest last day the notice can give me to answer?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO's written notice was given to you
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest last day the notice can set question` MEANS
    `asa the date` 14 `days after` `the day the notice was given to me`

-- s 14A(3) "must not be shorter"; s 14A(4): "A manner specified in a notice under subsection (2) must involve the use of a
-- service to which paragraph 51(v) of the Constitution applies" (postal, telegraphic, telephonic or other like services:
-- post, telephone, email, an online form). Either requirement failed is JUST FALSE (a flat negative, and "must").
@export The Agency's CEO has asked me in writing for information. Does the notice give me the time, and use the means of answering, that the Act requires?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO's written notice was given to you
      `the last day the notice gives me` IS A DATE @desc The last day by which the notice asks you to give the information
      `the notice asks me to answer by post, phone, email or online` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way the notice asks you to answer uses post, telephone, email, an online form or a like service (rather than, say, only in person)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the notice made as s 14A requires question` MEANS
    IF      DATE_SERIAL `the last day the notice gives me` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (`What is the earliest last day the notice can set question` `the day the notice was given to me`)
        AND `the notice asks me to answer by post, phone, email or online`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 14A(2) is a "request"; s 14A(5): "A person may comply with a request under subsection (2)." The Act sets no duty to
-- answer and no penalty. As a regulative rule: I MAY give the information within the period; not using a permission is
-- never a breach, so the rule ends FULFILLED whether I answer in time, late or not at all.
GIVEN `the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Agency party` `Agency act`
`s 14A(5) -- I may give the CEO the information within the period in the notice` `the period` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the person asked`
    MAY   `give the CEO the information asked for`
    WITHIN `the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- Fork line: s 14A(5) "may comply" read as no duty: JUST FALSE (the text puts the request and the permission in its own
-- words). The other reading is NOTHING (the Act is silent on a duty). Worked through the s 14A(5) rule: if the trace ends in
-- breach the answer would be JUST TRUE; a MAY rule never does.
@export The Agency's CEO has asked me for information. Must I give it, and am I in breach if I do not answer by the date in the notice?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO's written notice was given to you
      `the last day the notice gives me` IS A DATE @desc The last day by which the notice asks you to give the information
      `I have given the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the CEO the information asked for
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the information (ignored if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I give the CEO the information question` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 14A(5) -- I may give the CEO the information within the period in the notice` (`asa days from` `the day the notice was given to me` `to` `the last day the notice gives me`)) 0 `my events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `my events` MEANS
            IF `I have given the information`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `I, the person asked` `give the CEO the information asked for` (`asa days from` `the day the notice was given to me` `to` `the day I gave it`))
            ELSE LIST (EVENT `I, the person asked` `I check where things stand` (`asa days from` `the day the notice was given to me` `to` `today`))

-- s 14A(6): "Subsection (5) has effect despite anything in: (a) a law of the Commonwealth (other than this Act); or (b) a law
-- of a State or Territory." Where the request is one s 14A reaches (s 14A(1), (2)), giving the information is permitted
-- despite such a law: JUST TRUE. Where it is not a s 14A request, s 14A(5) and (6) do not speak: NOTHING.
-- Fork line: a contract or an equitable duty of confidence is not plainly "a law of the Commonwealth" or "of a State or
-- Territory"; taken as NOTHING. The other reading is JUST TRUE (the general law of a State is "a law of a State").
DECLARE `What might stop me` IS ONE OF
    `a Commonwealth Act or instrument other than this Act (such as the Privacy Act 1988)`
    `a State or Territory Act or instrument (such as a State health records or privacy law)`
    `a contract or a duty of confidence (not an Act)`
    `nothing`

@export The Agency's CEO has asked me for information that a privacy, secrecy or confidentiality rule might otherwise stop me giving. May I give it anyway?
GIVEN `the CEO believes on reasonable grounds I have relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO believes, on reasonable grounds, that you have information relevant to the Agency's work on the national asbestos and silica plans or its data on exposure (s 8(1)(a), (b), (g))
      `the CEO is satisfied the information is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO is satisfied the information is necessary for that work
      `the CEO is satisfied the information is not otherwise available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO is satisfied the information is not otherwise available to the CEO
      `the request is made by written notice given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request came to you as a written notice (a letter or an email)
      `what might stop me` IS A `What might stop me` @desc What might otherwise stop you giving the information: "a Commonwealth Act or instrument other than this Act (such as the Privacy Act 1988)", "a State or Territory Act or instrument (such as a State health records or privacy law)", "a contract or a duty of confidence (not an Act)", or "nothing"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I give the information despite another law question` MEANS
    IF `s 14A reaches me and the request` `the CEO believes on reasonable grounds I have relevant information` `the CEO is satisfied the information is necessary` `the CEO is satisfied the information is not otherwise available` `the request is made by written notice given to me`
    THEN CONSIDER `what might stop me`
         WHEN `a contract or a duty of confidence (not an Act)` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 31, 32, 34 -- can I be appointed to the Council (if you are seeking a place on the Council)`

-- s 31: the Council is the Chair; one member representing the Commonwealth; 4 representing State, Territory and local
-- governments; 2 representing the interests of workers; 2 representing the interests of employers; (ea) 1 member who has
-- expertise relevant to asbestos safety, asbestos-related diseases, silica safety or silica-related diseases; 2 other members.
DECLARE `Council place` IS ONE OF
    `the Chair (s 31(a))`
    `the member representing the Commonwealth (s 31(b))`
    `a member representing State, Territory and local governments (s 31(c))`
    `a member representing the interests of workers (s 31(d))`
    `a member representing the interests of employers (s 31(e))`
    `the member with relevant expertise (s 31(ea))`
    `one of the 2 other members (s 31(f))`

-- s 32(3): "A person is eligible for appointment as a Council member under paragraph 31(a), (d), (e) or (f) only if the
-- Minister is satisfied that: (a) the person has knowledge or experience in one or more of the following: [asbestos safety;
-- public health issues relating to asbestos; asbestos-related diseases; the representation of, or the provision of support
-- to, persons with asbestos-related diseases and their families; silica safety; silica-related diseases; the same for
-- silica-related diseases; financial management; corporate governance]; or (b) the person: (i) has, or has had, an
-- asbestos-related disease; or (ii) has lived experience as a family member, carer or advocate in providing support to a
-- person who has, or has had, an asbestos-related disease; or (iii), (iv) [the same for silica-related disease]."
-- s 32(4): a worker member "only if: (a) the person has been nominated for the appointment by an authorised worker body; and
-- (b) the Minister agrees to the person being appointed." s 32(7): the same for an employer member and an authorised employer
-- body.
-- "only if": a failed condition is JUST FALSE. Met conditions are read as JUST TRUE (fork line: the Act sets no other
-- condition; the other reading is NOTHING, the conditions being necessary only). For the Commonwealth and the State,
-- Territory and local government places the Act sets no condition: NOTHING. For the s 31(ea) place, the paragraph itself
-- describes a member "who has expertise": without it JUST FALSE, with it JUST TRUE (fork line; other reading NOTHING).
@export Am I eligible to be appointed to the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Council, for example as someone who has, or has cared for someone with, an asbestos-related or silica-related disease?
GIVEN `the place` IS A `Council place` @desc The place on the Council: "the Chair (s 31(a))", "the member representing the Commonwealth (s 31(b))", "a member representing State, Territory and local governments (s 31(c))", "a member representing the interests of workers (s 31(d))", "a member representing the interests of employers (s 31(e))", "the member with relevant expertise (s 31(ea))", or "one of the 2 other members (s 31(f))"
      `the Minister is satisfied I have relevant knowledge or experience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied you have knowledge or experience in asbestos or silica safety, public health issues relating to asbestos, asbestos- or silica-related diseases, representing or supporting people with those diseases and their families, financial management or corporate governance
      `the Minister is satisfied I have lived experience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that you have or had an asbestos-related or silica-related disease, or have lived experience as a family member, carer or advocate supporting someone who has or had one
      `I was nominated by an authorised body for the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a workers' or employers' place: whether a body the Minister has authorised to represent workers (or employers) nominated you for it
      `the Minister agrees to my appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a workers' or employers' place: whether the Minister agrees to your being appointed
      `I have expertise relevant to asbestos or silica safety or disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the expertise place: whether you have expertise relevant to asbestos safety, asbestos-related diseases, silica safety or silica-related diseases
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I eligible to be appointed to the Council question` MEANS
    `asa eligible for` `the place` `the Minister is satisfied I have relevant knowledge or experience` `the Minister is satisfied I have lived experience` `I was nominated by an authorised body for the place` `the Minister agrees to my appointment` `I have expertise relevant to asbestos or silica safety or disease`

GIVEN `the place` IS A `Council place`
      `knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `nominated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `expertise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`asa eligible for` `the place` `knowledge` `lived` `nominated` `agrees` `expertise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `the member representing the Commonwealth (s 31(b))` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a member representing State, Territory and local governments (s 31(c))` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the member with relevant expertise (s 31(ea))` THEN
        IF `expertise` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a member representing the interests of workers (s 31(d))` THEN `yes or no` (`s 32(3)` AND `s 32(4) or (7)`)
    WHEN `a member representing the interests of employers (s 31(e))` THEN `yes or no` (`s 32(3)` AND `s 32(4) or (7)`)
    OTHERWISE `yes or no` `s 32(3)`
    WHERE
        `s 32(3)` MEANS `knowledge` OR `lived`
        `s 32(4) or (7)` MEANS `nominated` AND `agrees`
        GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `yes or no` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 34(2): the Minister may appoint a person to act as a Council member (other than the Chair) during a vacancy or an absence.
-- s 34(3), (4): where the acting appointment is to a place under s 31(d), (e) or (f), "a person is not eligible for
-- appointment to act as that member unless the person is eligible for appointment as that member (see subsection 32(3))".
-- "not eligible ... unless": JUST FALSE when I am not eligible for the place itself. Fork line: for the workers' and
-- employers' places, "eligible for appointment as that member" is read to include the nomination and agreement of s 32(4) or
-- (7), the "(see subsection 32(3))" being a pointer only; the other reading tests s 32(3) alone. Once met, JUST TRUE (fork
-- line; other reading NOTHING). For the other places other than the Chair, s 34 sets no condition: NOTHING. Acting as Chair
-- is s 34(1), open to "a Council member" with no further test: NOTHING here (the Act sets no eligibility to answer).
@export Can I be appointed to act in a place on the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Council while it is vacant or its member is absent?
GIVEN `the place` IS A `Council place` @desc The place you would act in (see the eligibility question for the list)
      `the Minister is satisfied I have relevant knowledge or experience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied you have knowledge or experience in asbestos or silica safety, public health issues relating to asbestos, asbestos- or silica-related diseases, supporting people with those diseases, financial management or corporate governance
      `the Minister is satisfied I have lived experience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that you have or had an asbestos-related or silica-related disease, or have lived experience as a family member, carer or advocate supporting someone who has or had one
      `I was nominated by an authorised body for the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a workers' or employers' place: whether an authorised workers' (or employers') body nominated you
      `the Minister agrees to my appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a workers' or employers' place: whether the Minister agrees to your appointment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be appointed to act on the Council question` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `a member representing the interests of workers (s 31(d))` THEN `asa eligible for` `the place` `the Minister is satisfied I have relevant knowledge or experience` `the Minister is satisfied I have lived experience` `I was nominated by an authorised body for the place` `the Minister agrees to my appointment` FALSE
    WHEN `a member representing the interests of employers (s 31(e))` THEN `asa eligible for` `the place` `the Minister is satisfied I have relevant knowledge or experience` `the Minister is satisfied I have lived experience` `I was nominated by an authorised body for the place` `the Minister agrees to my appointment` FALSE
    WHEN `one of the 2 other members (s 31(f))` THEN `asa eligible for` `the place` `the Minister is satisfied I have relevant knowledge or experience` `the Minister is satisfied I have lived experience` `I was nominated by an authorised body for the place` `the Minister agrees to my appointment` FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `ss 33, 35 -- my term and my pay as a Council member (if you are appointed to the Council)`

-- s 33: "A Council member holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not be more
-- than 3 years." "must not be more": over 36 months is JUST FALSE.
@export I have been appointed to the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Council. Is the term in my instrument of appointment within what the Act allows?
GIVEN `months in my term` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the term in your instrument of appointment, in months
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my Council term within the limit question` MEANS
    IF `months in my term` AT MOST 36
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 35(1): "A Council member is to be paid the remuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal" (or, failing a
-- determination, prescribed by the rules). s 35(2): "However, a Council member is not entitled to be paid remuneration if he
-- or she holds an office or appointment, or is otherwise employed, on a full-time basis in the service or employment of:
-- (a) a State; or (b) a corporation (a public statutory corporation) that: (i) is established for a public purpose by a law
-- of a State; and (ii) is not a tertiary education institution; or (c) a company limited by guarantee, where the interests
-- and rights of the members in or in relation to the company are beneficially owned by a State; or (d) a company in which all
-- the stock or shares are beneficially owned by a State or by a public statutory corporation."
-- The Note points to s 7(11) of the Remuneration Tribunal Act 1973 for full-time Commonwealth or Territory service: not
-- deposited, so NOTHING.
DECLARE `My full-time work` IS ONE OF
    `full-time in the service or employment of a State`
    `full-time with a State public statutory corporation (not a tertiary education institution)`
    `full-time with a tertiary education institution established by a State law`
    `full-time with a State-owned company limited by guarantee`
    `full-time with a company wholly owned by a State or a State public statutory corporation`
    `full-time in the service of the Commonwealth or a Territory`
    `none of these (part-time public work, private work, self-employed, retired or not working)`

@export I am a member of the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Council. Am I entitled to be paid remuneration for it?
GIVEN `my full-time work` IS A `My full-time work` @desc Your other work, if any: "full-time in the service or employment of a State", "full-time with a State public statutory corporation (not a tertiary education institution)", "full-time with a tertiary education institution established by a State law", "full-time with a State-owned company limited by guarantee", "full-time with a company wholly owned by a State or a State public statutory corporation", "full-time in the service of the Commonwealth or a Territory", or "none of these (part-time public work, private work, self-employed, retired or not working)"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to Council remuneration question` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my full-time work`
    WHEN `full-time in the service or employment of a State` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `full-time with a State public statutory corporation (not a tertiary education institution)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `full-time with a State-owned company limited by guarantee` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `full-time with a company wholly owned by a State or a State public statutory corporation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `full-time in the service of the Commonwealth or a Territory` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 37(3) -- my disclosure of interests (if you are a Council member)`

-- s 37(1): a disclosure by a Council member under s 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 to
-- each other member "must be recorded: (a) in any advice provided, or recommendations made, to the CEO by the Council; and
-- (b) in any guidelines issued to the CEO by the Council." s 37(3): "the member is taken not to have complied with section
-- 29 of that Act if the disclosure is not recorded as required by subsection (1)".
-- "if": recorded as required is JUST FALSE (s 37(3) does not deem a failure; whether I otherwise complied with s 29 is a
-- question under the PGPA Act, not encoded). Not recorded is JUST TRUE, whoever failed to record it.
@export I am a Council member and disclosed an interest to the other members. Am I treated as not having complied with my duty to disclose interests?
GIVEN `my disclosure was recorded in the Council's advice, recommendations and guidelines to the CEO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disclosure was recorded in every piece of advice, recommendation and guideline the Council gave the CEO that s 37(1) requires it to be in (answer yes if the Council gave none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I taken not to have complied with the disclosure duty question` MEANS
    IF `my disclosure was recorded in the Council's advice, recommendations and guidelines to the CEO`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 39, 40 -- leaving the Council (if you are a Council member)`

-- s 39(1): "A Council member may resign his or her appointment by giving the Minister a written resignation." s 39(2): "The
-- resignation takes effect on the day it is received by the Minister or, if a later day is specified in the resignation, on
-- that later day." A day specified that is not later than receipt is not "a later day": receipt governs.
@export I want to resign from the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Council. On what day does my resignation take effect?
GIVEN `the day the Minister receives my written resignation` IS A DATE @desc The day the Minister receives your written resignation
      `my resignation names a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your resignation names a day on which it is to take effect
      `the day it names` IS A DATE @desc The day your resignation names (ignored if it names none)
GIVETH A DATE
`When does my Council resignation take effect question` MEANS
    IF      `my resignation names a day`
        AND DATE_SERIAL `the day it names` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the day the Minister receives my written resignation`
    THEN `the day it names`
    ELSE `the day the Minister receives my written resignation`

-- s 40: "The Minister may terminate the appointment of a Council member: (a) for misbehaviour; or (b) if the member is
-- incapable of performing the duties of his or her office; or (c) if the member: (i) becomes bankrupt; or (ii) applies to take
-- the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors; or (iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or
-- (iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the benefit of his or her creditors; or (d) if the member is
-- absent, except on leave of absence, from 3 consecutive meetings of the Council; or (e) if the member fails, without
-- reasonable excuse, to comply with section 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 ... or rules
-- made for the purposes of that section."
-- s 37(3) feeds (e): a disclosure not recorded is a failure to comply with s 29.
-- Any ground: JUST TRUE (the Minister may, not must). No ground: the list is not closed with "only", so NOTHING (fork line:
-- the other reading, JUST FALSE, treats the grounds as exhaustive, as termination grounds usually are read).
@export I am a member of the Asbestos and Silica Safety and Eradication Council. Can the Minister end my appointment?
GIVEN `the Minister finds misbehaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there has been misbehaviour on your part, as the Minister would have to find
      `I am incapable of performing my duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are incapable of performing the duties of the office
      `I have become bankrupt or entered an insolvency arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have become bankrupt, applied for relief under a bankruptcy or insolvency law, compounded with your creditors, or assigned your remuneration for your creditors' benefit
      `consecutive meetings I missed without leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest number of consecutive Council meetings you have been absent from without leave of absence
      `I failed to comply with my duty to disclose interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to comply with s 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 (disclosing material personal interests) or rules under it
      `my disclosure was recorded in the Council's advice, recommendations and guidelines to the CEO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every disclosure of interest you made was recorded in the Council's advice, recommendations and guidelines to the CEO as s 37(1) requires (answer yes if you made none or the Council gave none)
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable excuse for any failure to comply with the duty to disclose interests
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister terminate my Council appointment question` MEANS
    IF      `the Minister finds misbehaviour`
        OR  `I am incapable of performing my duties`
        OR  `I have become bankrupt or entered an insolvency arrangement`
        OR  `consecutive meetings I missed without leave` AT LEAST 3
        OR  (    (    `I failed to comply with my duty to disclose interests`
                  OR (NOT `my disclosure was recorded in the Council's advice, recommendations and guidelines to the CEO`))
             AND (NOT `I had a reasonable excuse`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
